# Somatic review routing

HIGH-RISK paths — ALWAYS require human/planner review, NEVER auto-approve:
- somatic/safety/**          (safety core: emergency screen, advisory framing, consent gate; + the phase12_contracts monolith)
- somatic/consent/**         (consent scopes + ledger — default-OFF is load-bearing)
- somatic/advisory/**        (AI adapter — network egress + SAFE_FALLBACK)
- somatic/insights/**        (no-hardcoded-medical-normals guard)
- somatic/flows/**           (the consent-gated end-to-end flows)
- somatic/fabric/** and any fabric JCS/Merkle conformance vectors   (frozen byte-interop)
- pyproject.toml dependencies   (MUST stay [])
- .github/workflows/**       (CI / release)

AUTO-APPROVE eligible (only if Bugbot + Security review are clean AND risk = Low):
- docs-only (**/*.md, docs/**, planning/**), test-only (tests/**), comment/format-only

ROUTING:
- Any PR touching a high-risk path -> Security Reviewer + human/planner review, never auto-approved. (The Fable 5 planner's host-verification IS that human review.)
- General code PRs -> Bugbot review; auto-approve if clean + Low risk.
- Bugbot is a limited resource: do not request it on PRs already auto-approvable by policy.
